 ScarStore contract exactly — propose_scar (including ScarQuarantined for signatures with fewer than MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS conditions), match_scars (subset signature match, sorted by id), get_precedent, injected_scars — but persists rows to a SQLite database file given at construction; ids must continue the scar-NNNN sequence across restarts (derive from max existing id); (2) wire it in ops/autonomous_run.py: construct SqliteScarStore(state_dir / 'scars.db') and pass it as SoftLoop's scar_store= parameter so EvolutionLayer (which takes loop.scar_store) writes durably; (3) tests in tests/runtime/test_sqlite_scar_store.py covering: a scar proposed in one store instance is visible in a fresh instance opened on the same file (cross-process persistence), quarantine semantics preserved, match_scars returns identical results to the in-memory store for the same data, and id sequence continues across restarts.\",\n 4 |     \"accept\": [\n 5 |       \"runtime/memory/sqlite_store.py exports SqliteScarStore with the full ScarStore contract, persistent to a SQLite file\",\n 6 |       \"ops/autonomous_run.py passes SqliteScarStore(state_dir / 'scars.db') into SoftLoop(scar_store=...)\",\n 7 |       \"tests/runtime/test_sqlite_scar_store.py proves cross-instance persistence, quarantine preservation, and match parity\",\n 8 |       \"uv run pytest -q tests/runtime/test_sqlite_scar_store.py passes\"\n 9 |     ],\n10 |     \"changed_paths\": [\n11 |       \"runtime/memory/sqlite_store.py\",\n12 |       \"ops/autonomous_run.py\",\n13 |       \"tests/runtime/test_sqlite_scar_store.py\"\n14 |     ],\n15 |     \"builder_evidence\": [\n16 |       {\n17 |         \"claim_id\": \"durable_scars\",\n18 |         \"command\": \"uv run pytest -q tests/runtime/test_sqlite_scar_store.py\",\n19 |         \"artifact_hash\": \"2c26b46b68ffc68ff99b453c1d30413413422d706483bfa0f98a5e886266e7ae\",\n20 |         \"exit_code\": 0,\n21 |         \"stdout\": \"passed\"\n22 |       }\n23 |     ],\n24 |     \"go