ing B; add EVOLUTION events from the EvolutionLayer chain).\n34 | \n35 | ## Execution constraint (notebook Entry 142 LIMITATION)\n36 | \n37 | GPT-5.6 Sol quota exhausted until ~2026-08-22 ⇒ intakes run **GLM-5.3-only**\n38 | (`autonomous_run.py … glm`). All seals from this window carry homogeneous-audit risk;\n39 | deterministic kernel guarantees (court reproduction, evidence binding, taint index,\n40 | junk-artifact filter, model attribution) remain fully in force. Re-run the proof intake\n41 | under `hybrid` when GPT quota returns and record the delta.","success":true},{"query":"/var/folders/b0/hb9_mxhn4nz09tzctglbjq6w0000gp/T/paeos-t-a730e3e834b5-xhykd82b/runtime/memory/__init__.py","result":"  1 | \"\"\"Scar store + signature matching (PAEOS-8 §10 B1.F / FR-6 / §7.1).\n  2 | \n  3 | \"No rule without a scar\": a failure becomes a **scar** — a lesson with a **detection signature** and\n  4 | a set of *conditions* (tags) under which it applies. A scar is **auto-injected** into a matching\n  5 | goal at the injection stages (`RE_DERIVE`, `DESIGN`, `CRITIQUE`, `VERIFY` — stages 0/7/8/11), so the\n  6 | system does not repeat the mistake (FR-6, always on the path).\n  7 | \n  8 | Matching is **subset containment**: a scar with conditions `{a, b}` applies to a goal whose\n  9 | signature is a superset (`{a, b, …}`) — precise, never firing on unrelated goals. Proposing a scar\n 10 | is a **gated transition** (T3/A-10), not a direct write: a scar whose signature is too broad (fewer\n 11 | than `MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS` conditions — it would inject *everywhere*) is **quarantined**, closing the\n 12 | scar-poisoning vector (T3). This module implements the B1.A `ScarBackend`.\n 13 | \"\"\"\n 14 | \n 15 | from __future__ import annotations\n 16 | \n 17 | from dataclasses import dataclass\n 18 | \n 19 | from kernel.types import StageId\n 20 | \n 21 | __all__ = [\n 22 |     \"INJECTION_STAGES\",\n 23 |     \"MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS\",\n 24 |     \"Scar\",\n 25 |     \"ScarDraft\",\n 26 |     \"ScarQuarantined\",\n 27 |     \"ScarStore\",\n 28 |     \"parse_signature\",\n 29 | ]\n 30 | \n 31 | # Scars are injected at these stages (PAEOS-8 §10: stages 0/7/8/11).\n 32 | INJECTION_STAGES: frozenset[StageId] = frozenset(\n 33 |     {StageId.RE_DERIVE, StageId.DESIGN, StageId.CRITIQUE, StageId.VERIFY}\n 34 | )\n 35 | \n 36 | # A scar must have at least this many conditions, else it is over-broad (T3 poison guard).\n 37 | MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS = 2\n 38 | \n 39 | \n 40 | class ScarQuarantined(Exception):\n 41 |     \"\"\"A proposed scar's signature is too broad to inject safely — quarantined (T3).\"\"\"\n 42 | \n 43 | \n 44 | @dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\n 45 | class ScarDraft:\n 46 |     \"\"\"A proposed scar (a gated transition, not a direct write — T3/A-10).\"\"\"\n 47 | \n 48 |     signature: frozenset[str]  # the conditions (tags) under which this scar applies\n 49 |     lesson: str\n 50 |     detection: str  # detection signature: how to catch this defect class next time (K6)\n 51 |     severity: str = \"medium\"\n 52 | \n 53 | \n 54 | @dataclass(frozen=True, slots=True)\n 55 | class Scar:\n 56 |     \"\"\"A recorded, matchable lesson.\"\"\"\n 57 | \n 58 |     id: str\n 59 |     signature: frozenset[str]\n 60 |     lesson: str\n 61 |     detection: str\n 62 |     severity: str\n 63 | \n 64 | \n 65 | def parse_signature(signature: str) -> frozenset[str]:\n 66 |     \"\"\"A goal/scar signature string (\"a,b,c\") to its tag set.\"\"\"\n 67 |     return frozenset(tag.strip() for tag in signature.split(\",\") if tag.strip())\n 68 | \n 69 | \n 70 | class ScarStore:\n 71 |     \"\"\"Stores scars and matches them to goals by signature. Implements the B1.A `ScarBackend`.\"\"\"\n 72 | \n 73 |     def __init__(self) -> None:\n 74 |         self._scars: dict[str, Scar] = {}\n 75 |         self._counter = 0\n 76 | \n 77 |     def propose_scar(self, draft: ScarDraft) -> Scar:\n 78 |         \"\"\"Accept a scar, or raise ScarQuarantined if its signature is too broad (T3).\"\"\"\n 79 |         if len(draft.signature) < MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS:\n 80 |             raise ScarQuarantined(\n 81 |                 f\"scar signature {set(draft.signature)} has < {MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS} conditions; \"\n 82 |                 \"too broad to inject — quarantined (T3)\"\n 83 |             )\n 84 |         self._counter += 1\n 85 |         scar = Scar(\n 86 |             id=f\"scar-{self._counter:04d}\",\n 87 |             signature=draft.signature,\n 88 |             lesson=draft.lesson,\n 89 |             detection=draft.detection,\n 90 |             severity=draft.severity,\n 91 |         )\n 92 |         self._scars[scar.id] = scar\n 93 |         return scar\n 94 | \n 95 |     def match_scars(self, signature: str) -> list[Scar]:\n 96 |         \"\"\"Scars whose conditions are all met by a goal with this signature (subset match).\"\"\"\n 97 |         goal_tags = parse_signature(signature)\n 98 |         matched = [scar for scar in self._scars.values() if scar.signature <= goal_tags]\n 99 |         return sorted(matched, key=lambda s: s.id)\n100 | \n101 |     def get_precedent(self, precedent_id: str) -> Scar | None:\n102 |         \"\"\"A scar by id, or None.\"\"\"\n103 |         return self._scars.get(precedent_id)\n104 | \n105 |     def injected_scars(self, *, signature: str, stage: StageId) -> list[Scar]:\n106 |         \"\"\"Matched scars to inject at this stage — empty unless `stage` is an injection stage.\"\"\"\n107 |         if stage not in INJECTION_STAGES:\n108 |             return []\n109 |         return self.match_scars(signature)","success":true}]}}
