e\": \"Contract drift between DurableScarStore and the in-memory ScarStore (match semantics, INJECTION_STAGES gating of injected_scars, match ordering, get_precedent) breaks L18 scar-injection assumptions or the existing in-memory store/tests\",\n      \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"axis\": \"accuracy/maintainability\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"HZ-03\",\n      \"title\": \"Scar ID instability across reopen: counter resets produce duplicate scar-NNNN ids, making get_precedent ambiguous and shadowing older lessons referenced from prior runs\",\n      \"severity\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"axis\": \"accuracy\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"HZ-04\",\n      \"title\": \"SQLite contention or corruption of state_dir/scars.db under ConcurrentScheduler parallel runs (multi-writer pressure, SQLITE_BUSY, partial writes)\",\n      \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"axis\": \"risk/latency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"HZ-05\",\n      \"title\": \"Latency/memory overhead: row load on construction plus write-through on every propose_scar adds file I/O to the hot loop vs the zero-cost in-memory dict\",\n      \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"axis\": \"latency/memory\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"HZ-06\",\n      \"title\": \"No schema migration path for scars.db if the scar record shape evolves (new columns, renames)\",\n      \"severity\": \"LOW\",\n      \"axis\": \"maintainability\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"HZ-07\",\n      \"title\": \"Unbounded scar corpus growth over long-lived operation inflates match_scars cost and matched injection payload size (_scar_refs CAS content per stage)\",\n      \"severity\": \"LOW\",\n      \"axis\": \"memory/latency\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"HZ-08\",\n      \"title\": \"Implementation and seal occur during the GLM-5.3-only interim window (GPT quota exhausted to ~2026-08-22): homogeneous-audit caveat applies to any seal from this window\",\n      \"severity\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"axis\": \"risk (execution environment)\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"safeguards\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SG-01\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-01\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"SAFETY_CONSTRAINT\",\n      \"description\": \"T3 quarantine gate preserved verbatim in DurableScarStore.propose_scar: any signature with fewer than MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS conditions raises ScarQuarantined BEFORE any durable write occurs — write-through only happens after the gate passes, so over-broad scars can never reach scars.db. Bound into the implementation contract: tests/runtime/test_scar_durability.py must prove quarantine still raises on a fresh instance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SG-02\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-01\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"SAFETY_CONSTRAINT\",\n      \"description\": \"Match semantics frozen to the existing subset-containment rule (scar.signature <= goal_tags via parse_signature): a durable scar can only inject into a goal whose signature is a SUPERSET of its conditions — precise, never firing on unrelated goals. Shared matching logic must be reused between ScarStore and DurableScarStore rather than reimplemented, so the two cannot drift apart.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SG-03\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-01\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"KILL_SWITCH\",\n      \"description\": \"scars.db is a plain SQLite file at state_dir/scars.db colocated with ledger.db: deleting the file is a complete, single-operation memory reset back to the zero-scar baseline, and reverting the ops/autonomous_run.py wiring (SoftLoop(scar_store=...) removed) restores today's in-memory behavior with no other code path affected. The intake is marked reversible=true for exactly this reason.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SG-04\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-02\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"SAFETY_CONSTRAINT\",\n      \"description\": \"Contract-parity freeze: DurableScarStore exposes exactly the ScarStore surface (propose_scar, match_scars, get_precedent, injected_scars) with identical semantics — injected_scars gated by INJECTION_STAGES (RE_DERIVE/DESIGN/CRITIQUE/VERIFY), match_scars sorted by id, get_precedent by id. The existing in-memory ScarStore and its tests (tests/runtime/test_scars.py, tests/runtime/test_evolution.py) must remain untouched and green; tests/runtime/test_scar_durability.py proves cross-instance persistence, quarantine preservation, and INJECTION_STAGES gating for the durable variant. Acceptance: uv run pytest -q tests/runtime/test_scar_durability.py tests/runtime/test_scars.py tests/runtime/test_evolution.py passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SG-05\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-03\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"SAFETY_CONSTRAINT\",\n      \"description\": \"ID stability rule: on construction the durable store loads existing rows and derives its counter from the max existing scar-NNNN id, so the sequence continues (never resets, never collides); once written, a scar's id is immutable. tests/runtime/test_scar_durability.py must assert that a scar proposed via one instance is returned with the SAME id by a fresh instance opened on the same file.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"SG-06\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-04\",\n      \"mechanism\": \"FALLBACK\",\n      \"description\": \"Concurrency handling follows the pattern already proven by the colocated ledger: SQLite's own file locking arbitrates cross-process access, and in-process L3 authoring is already single-committer (evolution_lock, IP-0005), so durable scar writes are serialized to one row-committed write per run. Downstream binding for L08/L11: build_scheduler constructs the durable store inside its existing state-dir bootstrap; if scars.db cannot be opened/created, construction must fail loud (consistent with the fail-loud invoker policy from the RB-0026 remediation phases) rather than silently degrading to an empty store that would masquerade as durable.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"accepted_risks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-01\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-04\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Residual SQLITE_BUSY risk under extreme cross-process parallelism is accepted: write volume is tiny (one durable write per run, post-gate), the ledger already runs SQLite under the same scheduler without corruption, and the kill switch (SG-03: delete scars.db) bounds worst-case blast radius to the scar corpus — never the ledger or CAS.\",\n      \"approver\": \"L07_MITIGATION_STAGE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-02\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-05\",\n      \"rationale\": \"I/O overhead accepted: the scar corpus is institutional lessons (O(runs), not telemetry — empirically zero scars exist today), match is O(n) subset containment identical to the in-memory store, and the stdlib-only constraint (no new dependencies) is honored by sqlite3. Latency is dominated by stage-model calls, not by a single-row INSERT.\",\n      \"approver\": \"L07_MITIGATION_STAGE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-03\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-06\",\n      \"rationale\": \"No migration path accepted: the schema is a single table introduced by this change with no legacy data to migrate (durability begins here — the audit proved zero scars ever persisted). Additive evolution is cheap (new nullable columns), and SG-03's delete-file kill switch remains the documented reset path if the schema ever needs a breaking change.\",\n      \"approver\": \"L07_MITIGATION_STAGE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-04\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-07\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Unbounded growth accepted for now: FR-6 subset-match gating means only scars whose conditions are all met inject into a given goal, bounding per-goal payload growth; scar lifecycle management (decay/compaction/promotion) is explicitly deferred to a follow-up intake rather than smuggled into this one (single-task session per AGENTS.md).\",\n      \"approver\": \"L07_MITIGATION_STAGE\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"AR-05\",\n      \"hazard_id\": \"HZ-08\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Homogeneous-audit window accepted per RB-0026 constraints: deterministic kernel guarantees (court reproduction, evidence binding, taint index, junk-artifact filter, model attribution, STAGE_COMPLETED attribution rows) remain fully in force and are model-independent; the proof intake must be re-run under 'hybrid' when GPT quota returns (~2026-08-22) and the delta recorded in the hallucination notebook (Entry 142 LIMITATION).\",\n      \"approver\": \"Founder-directed audit protocol (notebook Entry 142)\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","old_text":"null","path":"/var/folders/b0/hb9_mxhn4nz09tzctglbjq6w0000gp/T/paeos-t-a730e3e834b5-xhykd82b/mitigation/mitigation_catalogue_rb0026.json"}}}
