tics, `INJECTION_STAGES` gating, ordering, `get_precedent`) breaks L18 injection assumptions — or the change breaks the existing store/tests. |\n| HZ-03 | **HIGH** | accuracy | **Scar-ID instability across reopen.** A counter reset mints duplicate `scar-NNNN` ids, making `get_precedent` ambiguous and shadowing older lessons. |\n| HZ-04 | MEDIUM | risk/latency | **SQLite contention/corruption** of `state_dir/scars.db` under `ConcurrentScheduler` parallel runs (`SQLITE_BUSY`, partial writes). |\n| HZ-05 | MEDIUM | latency/memory | **I/O overhead**: full row load on construction + write-through on every `propose_scar` vs the zero-cost in-memory dict. |\n| HZ-06 | LOW | maintainability | **No schema migration path** for `scars.db` when the scar record shape evolves. |\n| HZ-07 | LOW | memory/latency | **Unbounded scar growth** inflates `match_scars` cost and `_scar_refs` injection payloads. |\n| HZ-08 | MEDIUM | risk (environment) | **Homogeneous-audit window**: implementation/seal run GLM-5.3-only until ~2026-08-22. |\n\n## Safeguards bound to hazards\n\n| ID | Hazard | Mechanism | Safeguard |\n|----|--------|-----------|-----------|\n| SG-01 | HZ-01 | SAFETY_CONSTRAINT | **T3 quarantine before any durable write.** `propose_scar` raises `ScarQuarantined` for signatures with `< MIN_SIGNATURE_TAGS` *before* write-through; over-broad scars can never reach `scars.db`. Proven by the durability test's quarantine case. |\n| SG-02 | HZ-01 | SAFETY_CONSTRAINT | **Subset-containment match frozen.** `scar.signature <= goal_tags` via `parse_signature`; a durable scar injects only into goals meeting ALL its conditions. Shared logic reused (not reimplemented) so the two stores cannot drift. |\n| SG-03 | HZ-01 | KILL_SWITCH | **Single-file memory reset.** `scars.db` is a plain SQLite file colocated with `ledger.db`; deleting it restores the zero-scar baseline, and reverting the `SoftLoop(scar_store=...)` wiring restores today's in-memory behavior. Blast radius never touches ledger/CA